./orchestration/tickets/T14-ui-foundation/plan-review.md:5:Two consecutive `codex exec` runs hung with zero output. Root cause found on the second: codex printed "Reading additional input from stdin..." — in a background shell stdin is an open pipe that never closes, so codex waited forever. Fix: `< /dev/null` on the relaunch. Total loss ~50 minutes. The team lead directed the pipeline to proceed: the orchestrator's sense-check (below) was written and the implementer dispatched while the stdin-fixed codex review runs in parallel; codex findings are dispositioned in this file when they land and any real ones are folded in before/with the diff review. The orchestrator had already independently verified the plan's load-bearing server-side claims (§ below) before proceeding, so the plan did not go to implementation unreviewed.
