./orchestration/tickets/T21-dogfood-skills/codex-plan-review-raw.txt:7865:SPEC.md:171:A single entry point (`plan`, installed via `pip install -e .` console script) speaking HTTP to the server. **The CLI is for agents (and developer debugging); the human never uses it — every human action lives in the UI.** No resolution verbs exist in it: accepting, approving, granting, unblocking, and day-plan decisions are UI/API-only. Global behavior: `--json` on every verb (machine output; stable exit codes: 0 success, 1 validation/domain error, 2 connection error); long text via `--body-file <path>` or `-` for stdin — body text is never passed as an inline argument; env defaults `PLAN_SERVER_URL`, `PLAN_TICKET_ID` (verbs taking a ticket id use it when omitted), `PLAN_RUN_ID`, `PLAN_CLAIM`, `PLAN_ACTOR`.
./orchestration/tickets/T21-dogfood-skills/codex-plan-review-raw.txt:7872:SPEC.md:257:- **DOCS.md** — plain-language documentation written progressively as each stage completes, never retrofitted. A smart non-engineer must be able to read it: what the planner is, the entities, how proposals and ceilings work, what the dispatcher does, how a day flows, what each screen shows, what the CLI verbs do, what the skills are for. If a section needs the code to be understood, rewrite the section.
./orchestration/tickets/T21-dogfood-skills/codex-plan-review-raw.txt:7883:   185	- REST JSON under `/api/`: CRUD + actions mirroring Section 8 verbs, PLUS the human actions that deliberately have no CLI form — accept/edit-accept with the grant pair, `needs_review` approve, unblock, grant changes, sprint create/freeze, day-plan accept/accept-all/invalidate/reject-all, drop — and `GET /api/board`, `GET /api/day/<date>`, `GET /api/sprint/current`, `GET /api/queues`. Every mutating endpoint routes through the same canonical functions (one writer per edge).
./orchestration/tickets/T21-dogfood-skills/codex-plan-review-raw.txt:7885:   187	- Test mode (Section 13): `POST /api/test/tick-boundary` and `POST /api/test/tick-dispatcher` run one tick synchronously; available only when test mode is on, else 404.
