./orchestration/tickets/W2-removals/impl-review.out:2011:./DOGFOOD.md:20:2. Seed wrinkle (same in every round, disclosed): on startup the real boundary job had already created a day row plus its bootstrap events and a `boundary_runs` row, so `plan seed --demo` refused with `db_not_empty` (naming the `days` table). As the human operator I cleared those three bootstrap tables (`DELETE FROM days; DELETE FROM events; DELETE FROM boundary_runs;` via sqlite3 on the scratch DB) and re-ran the seed, which then reported `{"sprints": 1, "sprint_items": 3, "tickets": 8, "links": 2, ...}`.
