./orchestration/tickets/W3a-status-systemb/plan-review.out:5501:orchestration/tickets/T15-day-review/impl-review-raw.txt:7067:orchestration/tickets/T15-day-review/impl-review-raw.txt:1668:   167	Every agent write (proposal, recap, heartbeat, run close) must carry `PLAN_RUN_ID` + `PLAN_CLAIM` matching the ticket's active claim, except proposal/recap writes from non-dispatched agent contexts (no claim env — e.g. the planner-main chat agent), which are permitted with the proposer taken from `PLAN_ACTOR` (default `agent`). Human writes happen through the UI/API only — the CLI is an agent tool. A write with a stale/foreign claim is rejected with a structured error naming the mismatch.
./orchestration/tickets/W3a-status-systemb/plan-review.out:5502:orchestration/tickets/T15-day-review/impl-review-raw.txt:7068:orchestration/tickets/T15-day-review/impl-review-raw.txt:1672:   171	A single entry point (`plan`, installed via `pip install -e .` console script) speaking HTTP to the server. **The CLI is for agents (and developer debugging); the human never uses it — every human action lives in the UI.** No resolution verbs exist in it: accepting, approving, granting, unblocking, and day-plan decisions are UI/API-only. Global behavior: `--json` on every verb (machine output; stable exit codes: 0 success, 1 validation/domain error, 2 connection error); long text via `--body-file <path>` or `-` for stdin — body text is never passed as an inline argument; env defaults `PLAN_SERVER_URL`, `PLAN_TICKET_ID` (verbs taking a ticket id use it when omitted), `PLAN_RUN_ID`, `PLAN_CLAIM`, `PLAN_ACTOR`.
./orchestration/tickets/W3a-status-systemb/plan-review.out:5503:orchestration/tickets/T15-day-review/impl-review-raw.txt:7070:orchestration/tickets/T15-day-review/impl-review-raw.txt:1686:   185	- REST JSON under `/api/`: CRUD + actions mirroring Section 8 verbs, PLUS the human actions that deliberately have no CLI form — accept/edit-accept with the grant pair, `needs_review` approve, unblock, grant changes, sprint create/freeze, day-plan accept/accept-all/invalidate/reject-all, drop — and `GET /api/board`, `GET /api/day/<date>`, `GET /api/sprint/current`, `GET /api/queues`. Every mutating endpoint routes through the same canonical functions (one writer per edge).
./orchestration/tickets/W3a-status-systemb/plan-review.out:5504:orchestration/tickets/T15-day-review/impl-review-raw.txt:7075:orchestration/tickets/T15-day-review/impl-review-raw.txt:1740:   239	Defaults the owner may override before the run; each is tagged where it binds: **R1** boundary hour 05:00. **R2** new-ticket grant `ceiling=needs_success, at_cap=propose`. **R3** spawn profile `default`, worker skill `planning-worker`. **R4** boundary evidence DB-internal only. **R5** replan serialization, latest-wins. **R6** seed excludes archives. **R7** max concurrent runs 2.
./orchestration/tickets/W3a-status-systemb/plan-review.out:5505:orchestration/tickets/T15-day-review/impl-review-raw.txt:7087:orchestration/tickets/T15-day-review/impl-review-raw.txt:1885:   120	- **Grant discipline** (when `requireGrant`): a local `sync()` sets `accept.disabled = inFlight || picker.getGrant() === null`. `sync` runs once at build (Accept starts disabled — nothing is picked) and is the picker's `onChange`. When `requireGrant` is false the button starts enabled (non-gating accepts carry no grant — resolution.py:174-187).
