./orchestration/tickets/W3a-status-systemb/plan-review.out:5533:orchestration/tickets/T15-day-review/plan-review-raw.txt:1639:orchestration/tickets/T15-day-review/plan.md:580:## 10. Execution order + self-checks (implementer runs fresh, in order)
./orchestration/tickets/W3a-status-systemb/plan-review.out:5534:orchestration/tickets/T15-day-review/plan-review-raw.txt:1757:    91	**Why this is not a client-side state store:** the no-store rule (SPEC §9, T14 doctrine) forbids caching/reconciling **canonical server data**. Chat messages are never stored server-side — `POST /api/chat/{id}/send` returns `{reply_text, session_key}` and persists only the session key (chat/service.py:64-104). The transcript is pure conversation-render state that exists nowhere else; losing it on page reload is correct (refresh restores server state, and the server has no transcript). Module scope survives WS-flush re-renders (scripts are not re-executed; only `route()` re-runs), which is exactly the survival mechanism: every re-render rebuilds the panel DOM from `chatTranscripts[entityId]`.
