./orchestration/tickets/W3a-status-systemb/plan-review.out:5817:orchestration/tickets/T14-ui-foundation/plan-review-raw.txt:2323:orchestration/tickets/T14-ui-foundation/plan-review-raw.txt:113:    43	SPEC §18.2's build check runs `node --check` on every file in `assets/`; `node --check` only parses JavaScript, and `assets/` legitimately holds CSS (`tokens.css`, required by §10). The instrument checks every `*.js` under `assets/` recursively — the only reading under which the required CSS can exist at all. Flagged by codex during the T02 implementation review; recorded here for the auditor.
./orchestration/tickets/W3a-status-systemb/plan-review.out:5818:orchestration/tickets/T14-ui-foundation/plan-review-raw.txt:2324:orchestration/tickets/T14-ui-foundation/plan-review-raw.txt:336:   185	- REST JSON under `/api/`: CRUD + actions mirroring Section 8 verbs, PLUS the human actions that deliberately have no CLI form — accept/edit-accept with the grant pair, `needs_review` approve, unblock, grant changes, sprint create/freeze, day-plan accept/accept-all/invalidate/reject-all, drop — and `GET /api/board`, `GET /api/day/<date>`, `GET /api/sprint/current`, `GET /api/queues`. Every mutating endpoint routes through the same canonical functions (one writer per edge).
