./orchestration/tickets/W3a-status-systemb/plan-review.out:12979:Keying `MindQueue` by `ticket_id` violates the W1/W3 carry-forward that continuing steps go through a per-session queue. The W1 queue contract says the key is the durable `session_key` at [queue.py](/Users/khushaljagota/.hermes/planning-v2/src/planner/minds/queue.py:6), and W3 says System B must separately serialize kickoff because two step-0 runs have no key. The plan’s 1:1 assumption is not enforced by schema; `chat_session_key` is just nullable text at [db.py](/Users/khushaljagota/.hermes/planning-v2/src/planner/core/db.py:70).  
./orchestration/tickets/W3a-status-systemb/plan-review.out:12980:Fix: keep `MindQueue` keyed by current non-null `session_key` for continuing runs, and add a System-B-owned ticket/kickoff serialization guard for `NULL` keys. Resolve the stored key inside that guard at execution time.
./orchestration/tickets/W3a-status-systemb/plan-review.out:12983:The plan deletes the dispatcher machine-lock with `dispatch/runtime.py`, contradicting the fix-spec’s “DECIDED KEEP” at [notes.md](/Users/khushaljagota/.hermes/planning-v2/orchestration/runtime-redesign/notes.md:194).  
./orchestration/tickets/W3a-status-systemb/plan-review.out:12984:Fix: relocate the reusable machine-lock helper out of `src/planner/dispatch/runtime.py` before deleting dispatch, and leave it available for W3b System A instead of dropping it.
./orchestration/tickets/W3a-status-systemb/plan-review.out:12995:The plan recognizes `alias` is load-bearing in the seed importer but misses that the same importer still inserts dropped columns. After removing `auto_blocked` and `consecutive_failures`, [importer.py](/Users/khushaljagota/.hermes/planning-v2/src/planner/seed/importer.py:232) will fail on fresh schema v3.  
./orchestration/tickets/W3a-status-systemb/plan-review.out:12996:Fix: update the seed ticket INSERT to omit `auto_blocked` and `consecutive_failures`; let `status` default to `empty` and `worker` default to `NULL`.
./orchestration/tickets/W3a-status-systemb/plan-review.out:13008:Keying `MindQueue` by `ticket_id` violates the W1/W3 carry-forward that continuing steps go through a per-session queue. The W1 queue contract says the key is the durable `session_key` at [queue.py](/Users/khushaljagota/.hermes/planning-v2/src/planner/minds/queue.py:6), and W3 says System B must separately serialize kickoff because two step-0 runs have no key. The plan’s 1:1 assumption is not enforced by schema; `chat_session_key` is just nullable text at [db.py](/Users/khushaljagota/.hermes/planning-v2/src/planner/core/db.py:70).  
./orchestration/tickets/W3a-status-systemb/plan-review.out:13009:Fix: keep `MindQueue` keyed by current non-null `session_key` for continuing runs, and add a System-B-owned ticket/kickoff serialization guard for `NULL` keys. Resolve the stored key inside that guard at execution time.
./orchestration/tickets/W3a-status-systemb/plan-review.out:13012:The plan deletes the dispatcher machine-lock with `dispatch/runtime.py`, contradicting the fix-spec’s “DECIDED KEEP” at [notes.md](/Users/khushaljagota/.hermes/planning-v2/orchestration/runtime-redesign/notes.md:194).  
./orchestration/tickets/W3a-status-systemb/plan-review.out:13013:Fix: relocate the reusable machine-lock helper out of `src/planner/dispatch/runtime.py` before deleting dispatch, and leave it available for W3b System A instead of dropping it.
./orchestration/tickets/W3a-status-systemb/plan-review.out:13024:The plan recognizes `alias` is load-bearing in the seed importer but misses that the same importer still inserts dropped columns. After removing `auto_blocked` and `consecutive_failures`, [importer.py](/Users/khushaljagota/.hermes/planning-v2/src/planner/seed/importer.py:232) will fail on fresh schema v3.  
