codex
I found one real race in the continuing path: queued resumes capture a session key before they actually run, so a rotated session key can make the next queued step resume the stale key, and can even split one ticket’s mind across two queue keys. I’m checking the prior F1-F6 wording now so the final verdict maps back to what was accepted.
