12974-1. `orchestration/tickets/W3a-status-systemb/plan.md:109`  
12975-The auto-accept seam is a real latent bug, not safely deferred. Current `file_proposal` auto-accepts and clears the proposal at [resolution.py](/Users/khushaljagota/.hermes/planning-v2/src/planner/tickets/logic/resolution.py:107), so System B’s “proposal present” check at plan line 99 will mark a successful real CLI proposal as `errored`. The direct DB proposal setup in `plan.md:253` masks this.  
12976:Fix: amend W3a so hermetic System B tests exercise the real ticket proposal writer during the fake run, and either handle auto-accepted proposals explicitly or move the gate change into W3a before shipping the literal invariant.
12977-
12978-2. `orchestration/tickets/W3a-status-systemb/plan.md:75`  
12979-Keying `MindQueue` by `ticket_id` violates the W1/W3 carry-forward that continuing steps go through a per-session queue. The W1 queue contract says the key is the durable `session_key` at [queue.py](/Users/khushaljagota/.hermes/planning-v2/src/planner/minds/queue.py:6), and W3 says System B must separately serialize kickoff because two step-0 runs have no key. The plan’s 1:1 assumption is not enforced by schema; `chat_session_key` is just nullable text at [db.py](/Users/khushaljagota/.hermes/planning-v2/src/planner/core/db.py:70).  
12980:Fix: keep `MindQueue` keyed by current non-null `session_key` for continuing runs, and add a System-B-owned ticket/kickoff serialization guard for `NULL` keys. Resolve the stored key inside that guard at execution time.
12981-
12982-3. `orchestration/tickets/W3a-status-systemb/plan.md:207`  
12983-The plan deletes the dispatcher machine-lock with `dispatch/runtime.py`, contradicting the fix-spec’s “DECIDED KEEP” at [notes.md](/Users/khushaljagota/.hermes/planning-v2/orchestration/runtime-redesign/notes.md:194).  
12984:Fix: relocate the reusable machine-lock helper out of `src/planner/dispatch/runtime.py` before deleting dispatch, and leave it available for W3b System A instead of dropping it.
12985-
12986-4. `orchestration/tickets/W3a-status-systemb/plan.md:56`  
12987-`session_key: str | ... = _UNSET` is a mypy/runtime typing trap, and the planned end write passes `result.session_key` from [runner.py](/Users/khushaljagota/.hermes/planning-v2/src/planner/minds/runner.py:41), which is `str | None`.  
12988:Fix: define a typed sentinel, e.g. `_Unset`/`_UNSET`, and annotate `session_key: str | None | _Unset = _UNSET`; only include `chat_session_key=?` when the value is not `_UNSET`.
12989-
12990-5. `orchestration/tickets/W3a-status-systemb/plan.md:74`  
12991-The test seam says to inject `FakeGateway.spawn`, but one `FakeGateway` is one child and is closed after one `run_step`; the fake documents this at [fake.py](/Users/khushaljagota/.hermes/planning-v2/src/planner/minds/fake.py:43). Multi-run tests in plan lines 245-249 will reuse a dead fake if implemented literally.  
12992:Fix: specify a test spawn sequencer that returns a fresh `FakeGateway` per spawn, and pass `spawn=sequencer.spawn`.
